Skies remain clear for the most part throughout the day. North Bay
terminals will be the most impacted by smoke from the Woodside Fire
on the Sonoma County coast. STS will experience visibility impacts
(~5-6SM) due to smoke through the TAF period meanwhile APC will see
more haze. Moderate onshore winds increase by the afternoon and ease
around sunset. A compressed marine layer around 1000 feet returns
this evening with high confidence in IFR ceilings at coastal
terminals (HAF, MRY, and SNS). Medium confidence on MVFR ceilings at
North Bay terminals. The amount of smoke in the air combined with
increasing 500 mb heights and a compressed marine layer, may allow
for sufficient subsidence to form MVFR ceilings. Interior South and
East Bay valleys remain VFR this TAF period.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR through the afternoon as westerly winds
increase. NW breezes off our coast increase overnight which may be
sufficient enough to push IFR ceilings over OAK and SFO. IFR
ceilings impact OAK first, followed by SFO around 07-10Z Saturday.
Medium confidence on exact timing of stratus arrival. Ceilings are
expected to mix out by mid-morning Saturday.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO. Stratus coverage may remain
more SCT008-010.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR through the day! Onshore breezes around
10-12 kt increase through the afternoon. Medium confidence on the
arrival of IFR ceilings tonight, though they are expected to arrive
at MRY first before filling in over SNS. Both terminals clear by mid-
morning Saturday.

