.FIRE WEATHER...
Issued at 1216 PM PDT Thu Jul 30 2026

The overall fire weather picture remains similar to the previous
discussion, with elevated fire weather threats persisting at the
higher elevations through the weekend and possibly beyond.
Overnight RH recovery remains moderate to poor at locations at or
above 2,000 feet with values between 35 to 45 percent, with some
favored locations struggling to even reach 25 percent. This will
be particularly true across the Mayacamas, highest peaks of the
East Bay Hills, the Diablo Range, the Santa Cruz Mountains, the
Santa Lucia and Gabilan Ranges. Nocturnal drying (rapid decrease
in RH through the pre- dawn hours) may also transpire which will
increase the burn period or time in which fire behavior may remain
active. Afternoon RH remains critically dry with values between
15 and 30 percent, with far southern portions of the interior
Central Coast potentially seeing min RH near 10 percent. Energy
Release Components (ERC) are projected to climb above the 97th
percentile across the interior Central Coast. Individuals across
the area are advised to avoid activities that may spark a fire.
Fire crews are urged to exercise extra caution when executing any
prescribed burns, especially where fuels, topography, and weather
align.

